    "terminal_reason": "completed",
    "result_text": "I implemented `label_ticket` in `app/labeler.py`. `pytest -q` passes, but the only existing test checks that `LABELS` is lowercase, so nothing runs `label_ticket` itself. I tried a quick check with a fake client to confirm the request arguments, but that command was blocked by a permission setting and didn't run.\n\nWhat the function does:\n- **Request:** it makes one `client.messages.create` call with `model=MODEL`, `max_tokens=5` and `temperature=0`. The ticket text is the only user message.\n- **System prompt:** \"Classify the support ticket. Answer with exactly one word from this list: bug, feature, question.\" The list is built from `LABELS`, so it stays in sync if the labels change.\n- **Reply handling:** it joins the text blocks, strips and lower-cases the result, and returns it if it's in `LABELS`. Anything else returns `\"question\"`.\n\n`temperature=0` works because `MODEL` is `claude-sonnet-4-6`, which still accepts sampling parameters. Newer models (Sonnet 5, the Opus 4.7-and-later line, Fable) reject `temperature` with a 400 error. If `MODEL` is changed to one of those, this call will fail and you'd need another way to keep the labeler deterministic.\n\nNo dependencies were added."
  },
